# DineAI Evaluation Layer Implementation Plan

Implement the lightweight, enterprise-quality evaluation layer for the DineAI Framework. This consists of two main testing components: **Integration Tests** and **End-to-End Tests**, located in `dine_ai/evaluations/integration_test.py` and `dine_ai/evaluations/end_to_end_test.py`.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The evaluation framework consists of:
> 1. **Integration Tests (`integration_test.py`)**:
>    * Sequential verification of all 11 DineAI pipeline modules (Schema Mapper, Validator, Feature Engineering, Text Builder, Embedding Builder, FAISS Builder, Semantic Search, Filtering, Ranking, Prompt Builder, Generator) to guarantee clean, exception-free communication, correct input/output types, shape checks, and warnings tracing.
>    * Executes end-to-end integration flows using synthetic/mock objects to avoid side-effects on primary datasets.
> 2. **End-to-End Tests (`end_to_end_test.py`)**:
>    * Simulates real user queries (e.g. keto, vegan, high protein, cheap, low calorie) traversing the full `DineAIApplication` orchestrator.
>    * Verifies search, filter passing, reordering, prompt builder templates, and final response compilation without crashes.
> 3. **Deterministic Constraints**:
>    * Both suites will run deterministically using the deterministic `MockProvider` and the dynamic `MockEmbeddingModel`, with zero dependencies on external APIs (never loading Qwen).
>    * Telemetry and health reports format results as PASS/FAIL indicators, overall percentages, and standard health rating terms (EXCELLENT, VERY GOOD, etc.).

